content.text:
Committed as `e47cb902` (1 ahead of origin; not pushed).

### What happens now

Sandbox already gone on Blaxel (`TERMINATED` / `DEACTIVATED` / `DELETED`). Caller does get or refresh:

```ts
const sandbox = await client.get("kit-example");
const info = await sandbox.refresh();

// BEFORE
// { id: "kit-example", state: "deleted", providerState: "DELETED" }
// terminal missing → if (info.terminal) never runs

// AFTER
// {
//   id: "kit-example",
//   state: "deleted",
//   providerState: "DELETED",
//   terminal: true,   ← set
// }
```

Same shape after `delete()` (unchanged), and same as Go:

```go
info, _ := instance.Refresh(ctx)
// State=Deleted, Terminal=true
```

So this polling pattern works in both languages:

```ts
const info = await sandbox.refresh();
if (info.terminal) {
  // stop retrying — resource lifecycle is done
}
```

Still **not** terminal: `DELETING` (in progress), `FAILED` → `error` (matches Go).

